ves a truth value unchanged; an odd number reverses it. We can therefore use decisive subexpressions rather than expand everything.\n\n- **(A) is false.** Its right-hand outer conjunct reduces to\n  \\[\n  ((F\\lor F)\\land \\cdots)\\ \\lor\\\n  \\neg\\bigl((T\\land T)\\lor(F\\lor F)\\bigr)=F.\n  \\]\n  Here:\n  - \\(6-(-4)=10\\not\\le6\\), and Yerevan is Armenia’s capital, so its triple negation is false.\n  - Triple-negated `False` is true, and \\(6-(-3)=9>3\\).\n  - \\(-8(9)+(-8)(-1)=-64\\le10=(-10)(-1)\\), so that comparison’s triple negation is false.\n\n- **(B) is false.** Its final conjunct is double-negated\n  \\[\n  -1(10)+3(10)\\le5(-10),\\qquad 20\\le-50,\n  \\]\n  which is false.\n\n- **(C) is false.** Its first disjunct contains \\(\\neg(T\\lor T)=F\\). Its second disjunct is the triple negation of an expression containing `not (False)` as a disjunct, so it is \\(\\neg T=F\\).\n\n- **(D) is true.** Inside the outer triple negation, a required conjunct is\n  \\[\n  7(-9)+9(6)>-4(-8),\\qquad -9>32,\n  \\]\n  which is false. Thus the outer triple negation is true. The remaining conjunct—double-negated “The capital of Afghanistan is Kabul”—is also true.\n\n- **(E) is false.** Its right-hand outer conjunct contains\n  \\[\n  \\text{not not}\\bigl(\\text{not}(\\cdots)\\land F\\bigr)=F.\n  \\]\n\nFinal answer: **(D)**."}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h","reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","store":false,"temperature":1,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":0}},"t